{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01418",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.04,
      "end_seconds": 7.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "Doctor, your next patient is here. I've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.77,
      "end_seconds": 14.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.73,
      "end_seconds": 27.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.94,
      "text": "doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps we came because of a dry cough in the evenings"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.51,
      "end_seconds": 33.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.88,
      "end_seconds": 46.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.61,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day. Moderate, really i'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.59,
      "end_seconds": 49.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.23,
      "end_seconds": 68.32,
      "duration_seconds": 17.09,
      "text": "Itchy eyes goes along with it, uh, most of the time. So, um, the Itchy eyes? That's been for two days. About Itchy eyes, a six out of ten, I suppose. It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.73,
      "end_seconds": 69.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.41,
      "end_seconds": 73.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "I've also had sneezing fits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.6,
      "end_seconds": 77.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.5,
      "end_seconds": 82.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "A three out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 82.84,
      "end_seconds": 94.29,
      "duration_seconds": 11.45,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse is 73 beats a minute, SpO2 99 percent on room air. Respiratory rate 15, blood pressure 113 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.63,
      "end_seconds": 96.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.45,
      "end_seconds": 103.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.59,
      "end_seconds": 115.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.34,
      "end_seconds": 118.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "right, nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.47,
      "end_seconds": 140.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Your chest is clear and your nose looks a little swollen inside."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.25,
      "end_seconds": 147.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Any wheeze or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.26,
      "end_seconds": 151.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Actually, no, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.19,
      "end_seconds": 154.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "have you had any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.68,
      "end_seconds": 157.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "No. No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 158.76,
      "end_seconds": 163.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.28,
      "end_seconds": 171.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.1,
      "end_seconds": 179.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.16,
      "end_seconds": 182.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "nothing else aches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.49,
      "end_seconds": 187.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 187.58,
      "end_seconds": 201.62,
      "duration_seconds": 14.04,
      "text": "She is on lansoprazole, 30 milligrams, before breakfast, I give it to her. She is on fluoxetine, every morning for my mood, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.95,
      "end_seconds": 205.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 207.22,
      "end_seconds": 215.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "It's, It's 20 milligrams. Right, she takes Glycomet, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.97,
      "end_seconds": 218.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "and what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 218.85,
      "end_seconds": 221.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "It's, It's 500 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.36,
      "end_seconds": 236.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.9,
      "end_seconds": 245.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "I've had acid reflux, yes i've had depression, yes i have diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.9,
      "end_seconds": 248.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.29,
      "end_seconds": 257.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "Okay, I can see acid reflux and depression in your file as well. Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.29,
      "end_seconds": 261.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.89,
      "end_seconds": 264.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.13,
      "end_seconds": 271.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.63,
      "end_seconds": 274.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.43,
      "end_seconds": 278.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.72,
      "end_seconds": 282.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Right, is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.48,
      "end_seconds": 287.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.09,
      "end_seconds": 290.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.01,
      "end_seconds": 296.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "no, I'm not allergic to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 297.34,
      "end_seconds": 306.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "Actually, I remember she had some kind of reaction to naproxen before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.46,
      "end_seconds": 313.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.97,
      "end_seconds": 318.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Fair enough, I'll write down both versions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.33,
      "end_seconds": 342.97,
      "duration_seconds": 15.64,
      "text": "okay, thinking it through, I'd lean towards seasonal hay fever causing the cough. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Early asthma is also on my list"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.28,
      "end_seconds": 348.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Let me think, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.22,
      "end_seconds": 385.46,
      "duration_seconds": 35.24,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's seasonal hay fever causing the cough, and we'll watch how it goes. What I'm giving you is fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, for the season. That should help with hay fever. Keep windows closed on high-pollen days and wash your hair at night. The thing that would worry me is if you start wheezing. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.15,
      "end_seconds": 391.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "book a review in a month does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.33,
      "end_seconds": 396.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}